# Vakter — vakter.app
# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify _redirects
#
# Syntax: <from>  <to>  <status>
# Cloudflare Pages docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
# Netlify docs:          https://docs.netlify.com/routing/redirects/
#
# ─── /download ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Phase 1 placeholder: points at the GitHub Releases "latest" asset path.
# GitHub redirects this to the actual versioned URL automatically.
#
# TODO (Phase 2 / Feature #14): once a Cloudflare R2 or a signed CDN URL
# is set up, replace this target with the canonical CDN URL so downloads
# don't bounce through GitHub's redirect chain. Update the status to 302
# until the CDN URL is stable, then switch to 301.
#
# Note: this URL will 404 until the first GitHub Release is published.
# Create a release tagged e.g. v1.0.0 with a Vakter.dmg asset attached,
# then this redirect will resolve correctly without any change here.
/download  https://github.com/jonathangebru/vakter/releases/latest/download/Vakter.dmg  302

# ─── Canonical trailing-slash redirects ───────────────────────────────────────
# Ensure /press and /concepts always resolve to their directory index.
# 301 is safe here — these paths will not move.
/press     /press/     301
/concepts  /concepts/  301

